BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:161778@iso-ne.com
DTSTAMP:20260227T004847Z
DTSTART:20260311T203000Z
DTEND:20260311T213000Z
SUMMARY:Intro to ISO with ISO-NE External Affairs
LOCATION:Teams
DESCRIPTION:ISO New England’s (ISO-NE) External Affairs department will host an Intro to ISO webinar on the evening of March 11. The webinar will provide an overview of ISO New England and our three critical roles and an opportunity for questions\, as time allows. This event is designed for a non-technical audience to learn about ISO New England. This session is free and open to the public.\n\nFor more information on ISO New England’s three critical roles\, see the following resources: \n\n\n	About Us: What We Do webpage\n	The Creation of ISO New England video\n	We Are ISO video\n\n\nThe ISO’s External Affairs department maintains regular communication with state regulators and policymakers\, state and federal legislators\, governors\, attorneys general and consumer representatives in the six states served by ISO New England to provide information on the wholesale electricity markets and regional power system.\n\nAdd to My Calendar\n\nThis event will be held virtually via Teams:\n\nJoin: https://teams.microsoft.com/meet/26059108715083?p=wVWFEpdKIcqFA9xxEk\n\nMeeting ID: 260 591 087 150 83\n\nPasscode: Wn9M24BG\nContact: Kerry Schlichting (kschlichting@iso-ne.com)\nhttps://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=161778
URL:https://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=161778
END:VEVENT
